        {
          "id": "F1_5",
          "source_id": "part1",
          "source_sha256": "4b1b09addb5ad3cab6dc885fb4f0a805fede65b2eecc8976b232e180a427edb9",
          "start": 1312,
          "end": 1500,
          "quote": "In American culture, when\nyou receive a compliment,\nit's very natural for\nyou to say thank you.\nFor example, your\nChinese is very good.\nYou say, thank you.\nYour English is good.\nThank you.",
          "topic": "美国文化中接受赞美的自然回应",
          "claim": "讲者以美国文化为例，说明收到赞美时很自然会说谢谢，例如别人说你的中文很好，你回答谢谢。",
          "evidence_indices": [
            56,
            57,
            58,
            59,
            60,
            61,
            62,
            63,
            64
          ],
          "attribution": "HAOHSIANG LIAO",
          "importance": "support",
          "attribution_start": 0,
          "attribution_end": 14
        },
        {
          "id": "F1_6",
          "source_id": "part1",
          "source_sha256": "4b1b09addb5ad3cab6dc885fb4f0a805fede65b2eecc8976b232e180a427edb9",
          "start": 1501,
          "end": 1872,
          "quote": "However, being humble\nis the way when\nyou receive a compliment\nin Chinese culture.\nYou don't accept it\nby saying thank you.\nSometimes you say things,\nfor example, like,\nthere's still a long way for\nme to go, so it's too far.\nOh, I don't know where the\ncompliments come from. [LAUGHS]\nSo yeah, the fundamental\nidea in Chinese culture\nabout compliments\nis to remain humble.",
          "topic": "中国文化中收到赞美时保持谦逊",
          "claim": "讲者表示在中国文化中收到赞美时，保持谦逊是方式，不会用谢谢来接受，有时会说还有很长的路要走、不知道赞美从何而来等；讲者认为中国文化关于赞美的根本观念是保持谦逊。",
          "evidence_indices": [
            65,
            66,
            67,
            68,
            69,
            70,
            71,
            72,
            73,
            74,
            75,
            76,
